      "locked": false,
      "text": "- decouple system.\n- push vs pull -> no simple answer depend on usecase.\n- kafka vs rabbitmq vs sqs ?? not sure about rabbitmq arch, let say taken kafka\n- Topic: <> , partition <> , replication factor <> , multiple brokers, availability zone, retention.\n- ordering -> partition key. \n- duplication -> if producer didn't send its okk, else better to use idenpotency at consumer\n  or we can use kafka transaction as well while pushing data to kafka for exactly one.\n- atleast -> pushing retry until succeed.  atmost one -> no retry.\n- scaling -> no. of brokers\n- lag monitor, cpu monitor, etc.\n \n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- decouple system.\n- push vs pull -> no simple answer depend on usecase.\n- kafka vs rabbitmq vs sqs ?? not sure about rabbitmq arch, let say taken kafka\n- Topic: <> , partition <> , replication factor <> , multiple brokers, availability zone, retention.\n- ordering -> partition key. \n- duplication -> if producer didn't send its okk, else better to use idenpotency at consumer\n  or we can use kafka transaction as well while pushing data to kafka for exactly one.\n- atleast -> pushing retry until succeed.  atmost one -> no retry.\n- scaling -> no. of brokers\n- lag monitor, cpu monitor, etc.\n \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
